## 42. E-Commerce Design

### Product Browsing

Use eventual consistency and caching.

Temporary stale descriptions or images are normally acceptable.

### Shopping Cart

Use session consistency or read-your-writes consistency.

The user should immediately see their cart changes.

### Checkout Inventory

Use strong consistency and ACID transactions.

The system must prevent overselling.

### Payment Processing

Use:

- Strong consistency
- ACID transactions
- Idempotency keys
- Durable transaction records

### Recommendations

Use eventual consistency because recommendations can be generated asynchronously.

### Analytics

Use weak or eventual consistency because small delays normally do not affect correctness.

### Recently Viewed Products

Use eventual consistency because this data is non-critical and replayable.

---

## 43. Social Media Design

### Post Creation

Use read-your-writes so the author immediately sees the new post.

Feed propagation can remain eventually consistent.

### Like Counts

Use eventual or weak consistency because temporary differences are acceptable.

### Comment Ordering

Use causal consistency when comments and replies depend on earlier content.

### Profile Updates

Use read-your-writes for the owner and eventual consistency for other viewers.

### Feed Generation

Use eventual consistency because availability, latency, and global scale are more important than exact immediate updates.

### Account Security Events

Use strong consistency because stale security data creates serious risk.

